Consider two modes or readout channels $x$ and $y$ in the same frame $F$: $$\frac{E_x}{E_F}=\frac{\omega_x}{\omega_F},\qquad
\frac{E_y}{E_F}=\frac{\omega_y}{\omega_F}.$$ Taking the ratio removes the reference unit: $$\boxed{
\frac{E_x}{E_y}
=\frac{E_x/E_F}{E_y/E_F}
=\frac{\omega_x/\omega_F}{\omega_y/\omega_F}
=\frac{\omega_x}{\omega_y}.
}$$ This is the important newly connected result. The same dimensionless ratio is obtained whether the intermediate bookkeeping is carried out in the zero frame or in the local frame, provided both channels are transformed through the same declared frame dictionary.

